WEBVTT

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.570
Ah, that's a charm for easy childbirth.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.610
I know that!

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.880
Milady, I beg you not to get carried away while we're in Japan.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.170
Alfred, I'm counting on you to pick me up, okay?

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.680
Teppei-sama?

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:57.110
You and Houjouin-sama did splendidly yesterday.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:02.140
Now that I think about it, I didn't really do much.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.360
In the end, it was just a story about Grandfather.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.110
If you do your best to accomplish your goals,

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.110
then I don't think you'll do wrong.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.320
Could it be that you're trying to comfort me?

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.990
Ah, no!  I didn't mean to...

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.490
Thanks, though.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.680
It's nothing.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:43.260
Arima-san!  I've been waiting for you!

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.040
Ah, you startled me!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.200
Do you have any plans for the holiday?

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.100
The upcoming holiday, I mean.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.100
Teppei-sama, I don't believe you have anything scheduled.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.560
Ah, really...thanks.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.270
So, what about the holiday?

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:04.450
I thought I should express my gratitude for filling in for me at the interview.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.580
Ah, don't worry about it.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.450
No way!  I must repay my debt without fail!

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.830
Hey!  Don't get so close!

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:16.810
If you don't accept my gratitude, I'll get even closer!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.470
I get it, I get it, so stop already!

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.780
It's great that you understand.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.250
Allow me to repeat myself.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.920
On the upcoming holiday, allow my to express my gratitude...

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.250
You've already expressed your gratitude quite well.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:32.310
If you would lend me your ear regarding this party you're worried about,

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.690
I'll gladly help you plan it.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.460
No way!  You'll consult with me?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.120
Yes, if it would please you, I'll gladly help you out.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.560
That's how I thought I could repay my debt.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.940
You can do such a thing?

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.590
Yes, of course!

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.410
Hey, that's a bad idea!

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:54.760
No, no, no.  This is something concealed behind this pure and innocent world.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.510
High schoolers doing that kind of thing,
no matter how you put it...

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.250
That means you'll be able to see all sorts of things, right?

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:06.100
I thought of that, too.  They'll be wearing something like this.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.160
Nooooo!

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.390
That's definitely suspicious!

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.730
If everyone is suspicious, then there's nothing to fear.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.480
Doooon't!

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.420
I guess you're right about that...

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.300
Great, isn't it?

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.020
What should I do...?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:26.280
Arima-sama, acting properly is not what matters.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.970
It's the experience that matters.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.160
I-Is that so?  I guess you're right...

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.650
Shall we give it a try?

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.500
Where are you guys going?

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:44.100
Teppei, are you going to be free for the holiday?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.690
...and that's how it is.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:52.490
Please, Silvie.  Would you lend me Teppei?

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:55.120
Why do you need my approval?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.740
You can do as you please.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:00.790
I can't do that.  After all, he's your fiancé, right?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.510
I-I still haven't accepted that yet!

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.780
I haven't spoken with him much recently.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.260
I see.  Then, it's okay.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.190
You see, I promised to go and play with Teppei.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.920
Ah!  Keep it a secret from my butler, okay?

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:22.010
If I go running off somewhere, I think he'll try contacting you.

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:25.350
In other words, you're asking me to cover it up for you?

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.550
Could you?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.000
I don't mind.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.030
Thanks, Silvie!  I'm so glad you're my childhood friend.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.900
Geez, how noisy.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:39.880
It's because of that pig.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.660
It's fine if she's just going out to have fun.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:47.610
However, I wonder if she's just ignoring Teppei's feelings and dragging him around?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.890
Seika-sama, do you have a fever?

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:53.120
Hm?  Did I say something weird?

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.750
You haven't spoken about Teppei-kun today.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.760
Did you get into a fight?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.890
It's not really a fight.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.330
I don't talk about Teppei-dono that often in the first place!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.960
What are you saying?

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:21.630
You're always talking about him after school, like, "Today, Teppei-dono..."

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.110
Maria!

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:28.490
At any rate, I'm glad you're becoming more conscious of the fact you're his fiancée.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:33.430
That's not it!  He's just a friend that studies swordsmanship, like I do.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.810
For me to become his fiancée...

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.440
Besides, if our relationship becomes any different...

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.110
You'll be unable to return to our homeland?

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:43.930
Silvie?

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:51.400
It's true that the Fil'mish Kingdom is in a rather delicate situation.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:56.020
I'll say it as many times as it takes.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.720
I want you to be happy in this peaceful country.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:00.450
I...

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:07.400
If you two can achieve happiness, it's okay to forget about our home country.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:12.070
You can forget about your mother and I as well.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:15.330
I honestly believe that.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:24.900
Father, I'm not feeling well at the moment.  Please excuse me.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.310
Ah, I see.  A 'blue day'?

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.530
A 'blue day'?  What's that?

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.270
It's that time of the month when something red---

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:35.100
It's not blue, red, or yellow!

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.600
So it's true?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.770
Alfred, you're persistent!

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.600
How many times do I have to repeat it?

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.890
Until I am satisfied.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.890
Are you truly going to Silvia-dono's house?

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:57.460
That's right, I am!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:00.950
It's not Arima's heir, is it?

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:05.480
Nothing of the sort!  Besides, why are you so critical of him?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.950
It is because I worry about you, Milady.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:12.010
I have heard rumors of you two getting too close at school.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.570
Rumors?  From whom?

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.870
Let's just say I have my sources.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.560
Just who exactly are your sources?

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.650
Who is it from?

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.420
Silvie!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:30.020
Hello?  I'm counting on you tomorrow, okay?

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.110
Silvie?

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:37.100
What's wrong?

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.090
Hello?

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.390
Teppei-dono...

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.370
Take care of Teppei-dono.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.960
Even calling Charlotte...

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:58.100
...what was I trying to say?

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:24.430
Teppei!

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.720
Sorry for being a little bit late.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:34.300
That's fine.  I wanted to try meeting like a normal boy and girl.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.520
Really?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:37.890
Thanks for waiting!

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:41.630
You're late!  I was just about to go home!

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:43.650
Something like that?

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:47.220
You were perfect.  Is the place you want to go far away?

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.700
That's true,

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.160
it's far, but we'll get there quickly.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.730
"It's far, but we'll get there quickly."  Where?

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:54.270
Osaka!

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:03.520
It's really close by!  Japan is so compact, I love it!

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.430
"It's far, but we'll get there quickly."

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:16.800
This feels great!

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.170
You're right.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:23.370
I wanted to come to a place where I wouldn't feel so confined.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.430
Neither my butler nor my bodyguard are here.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.630
I guess you usually have a bodyguard.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.320
You're a princess, after all.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.860
Bad Teppei!

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.860
"Bad?"  What is?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.710
Calling me "Princess" today is prohibited!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.850
Your response?

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:43.590
I understand!  I shall not call you "Princess" today!

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.300
Is that enough?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.570
Very well.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:54.000
However, I was wondering if you'll be okay without a bodyguard.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.110
Don't you feel uneasy?

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.560
I'll be fine!

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:59.240
I wonder where that confidence comes from...

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.900
I'll be fine if you're with me.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.980
You'll definitely protect me.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:09.630
That is, if it ever comes to it, right?

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.000
Understood.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.140
I've been stressed out about the party, so a change of scenery will do me good.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.920
Let's go all out!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.020
Yeah!

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.020
Teppei.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:45.200
I want it.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.410
The talking one.  I want it!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.210
Ah, Princess!  That's...

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:53.020
Calling me "Princess" is forbidden!

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:56.120
More importantly, acting like a princess is forbidden!

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.860
Noooo!  Don't lick my nose!

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:07.150
I'm going to lick your nose again!

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:11.660
Teppei!

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.610
Ah, that smells really good!

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.520
It's takoyaki.  See, the shop's right over there.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:21.910
Note: Takoyaki are deep-fried octopus dumplings.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.910
Takoyaki?

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.910
Don't tell me you've never had any?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.620
So, this is what they call takoyaki.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.930
Have you ever had something with this kind of sauce on it?

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:39.060
Of course I have!  Don't treat me like I'm stupid.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:45.570
It tastes good, but at the same time, it's really hot!

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:47.530
How was it?

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:49.410
It was delicious!

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.540
I'm glad you liked it.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:59.920
Does the chef in your house make takoyaki?

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:03.300
Huh?  No, we didn't have a chef or anything.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.090
Eh?  Then, who made your meals?

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:10.040
Mom used to make them a long time ago.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.910
Your mother?  How great!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:19.830
Having a chef is nice, but food prepared by your mother is special, isn't it?

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:22.050
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.020
That's how it was.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:29.230
Ah, I would like to try your mother's cooking.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.980
"Your mom is a great cook,"

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:34.170
was what they all said.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:37.020
Ah!  Let's get on that, Teppei!

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:40.030
She doesn't listen to a word I say...

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:55.780
You're a great person, Teppei.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:57.410
What's that for?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:02.990
I get the feeling that you love your mom from the way you talk about her.

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:05.740
That's why I think you're a great person.

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:07.110
Charl...

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:14.850
You're right.  I loved Mom a lot.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.840
"Loved?"

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.610
I haven't told you about it yet, have I?

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.000
My mom...died,

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.900
together with my dad.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.220
That's why I came to live with Grandfather.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:29.230
Teppei?

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:43.010
Look, Teppei.  It's so pretty.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:44.870
Yeah.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:50.380
Don't say, "loved".

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:54.070
Don't say you "loved" them.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:16:01.650
Your mother and father are still inside your heart,

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:04.010
and you're alive.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:11.520
As long as you're alive, the feelings you have for those you hold dear

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:13.750
will never become things of the past.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.880
Thank you.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.290
What's wrong?

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:32.160
It got cold when I wasn't paying attention.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:34.850
I...hate winter.

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:39.510
Even so, the winter in Japan isn't too bad.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.300
Eating stew sitting at a table with heater,

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.210
snowball fights,

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.440
playing on sleds,

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.720
making a snowman,

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.980
putting up a tree at Christmastime,

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:50.950
and once that's over, putting away the decorations.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:52.050
Then comes the new year.

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:54.530
Winter in Japan...

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.750
That's right, winter in Japan.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:00.390
When the leaves fall off the trees

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:03.190
and winter comes around,

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.010
you'll have to teach me about all of those things.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.710
If you'll teach me how to have fun,

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:12.750
I'm sure I'll come to like winter in Japan.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:15.360
Yeah, that's fine.  I promise you.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.190
Is it really, really a promise?

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.760
I told you that's fine.

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:26.500
All right, it looks like I'll be busy this winter!

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.130
Teppei?

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:33.960
Are you going to get married to Silvie?

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.060
I don't know.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.060
She's a nice girl.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:49.210
A long time ago, when both of our home countries got along,

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:52.140
we often played together.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:56.670
Silvie!  Stop scribbling like that!

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:00.030
Silvie!

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:02.320
If it's small, she won't be able to see it.

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:07.000
Hmm, I can't imagine her doing something like that.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:09.390
She may not look it, but she's pretty stubborn.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.370
What I didn't know was that...

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:18.140
...earlier that year, Silvie had lost her mother in an accident.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.050
Come in.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:24.820
What is it?

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:26.860
The young lady...

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:28.730
Silvie?  What did she do?

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:32.140
She told me to keep it a secret, but,

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:36.050
she asked me to make sure it was delivered to God.

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.200
What was written inside?

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:48.160
"Dear God, Silvie will be a good girl.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:52.030
So please, hurry up and give Mommy back."

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:56.080
"Mommy, hurry up and come home!"

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:00.030
Daddy?

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.220
Silvie.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:04.220
Why are you crying?

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.620
It'll be okay.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.630
Mommy will come back soon, okay?

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.020
Silvie...

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.490
I'm giving this to you.

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:36.330
It's okay, Daddy.  I remember Mommy's face.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:43.050
Dad, you're crying again...

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:52.160
I thought the rich were able to indulge themselves as they pleased.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:54.780
However, Grandfather and Seika-san,

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.190
Silvie and you,

00:19:57.190 --> 00:20:03.610
compared to where I was, it seems more inconvenient and probably lonelier.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:08.470
Of course, it's not the same for everyone.

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:14.880
It just feels like the loss would seem greater.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.200
I don't know what I'm trying to say.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.520
I think I understand, somehow.

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.550
What is it?

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:35.440
I just got an idea about the party I'm hosting!

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:36.600
Really?

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:41.440
Yeah.  To entertain everyone, I'll host a party that no one else could pull off.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.590
It's all because of you.  Thanks!

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:44.890
That's not it.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:49.520
I'll just spread my wings a little to come and have fun with you.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:55.010
All right, just watch me!  I'll throw an amazing party and surprise everyone!

00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:02.700
Like I said, don't hug me so suddenly like that...

